  <static seed="203" source="Contrib/DMOI/2-Sequences/2_3-Polynomial_Fitting/2_3_1.pg">
    <statement><p>Use polynomial fitting to find the formula for the <m>n</m>th term of the sequence <m>(a_n)_{n \ge 0}</m> which starts,</p>
<p><m>{0, 5, 14, 27, 44, 65}, \ldots</m></p>
<p><m>a_n =</m> <fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2n^{2}+3n</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>a_n = {2n^{2}+3n}\text{.}</m> Here we know that we are looking for a quadratic because the second differences are constant. So <m>a_n = an^2 + bn + c\text{.}</m> Since <m>a_0 = 0\text{,}</m> we know <m>c= 0\text{.}</m> So just solve the system</p>
<p><m>\begin{aligned}
{5} \amp  = a + b\\
{14} \amp  = 4a + 2b
\end{aligned}</m></p>
<p>to find <m>a = 2</m> and <m>b = 3</m>.</p>
</solution>
